<p>
  <b>{$summary}</b> - {$verdict}
</p>

<p>
  Each group states, case by case, the output the engine is supposed to produce. These suites
  assert; the manual only demonstrates, so a change that quietly alters a result still renders
  there and still looks right. Cases live in
  <code>apps/regression/sandbox/_cases/</code>, and
  <code>_cases/README.md</code> records what this kind of suite cannot check.
</p>

<p>
  A case here is a template rendered inside this request, which is quick and self-contained but
  is not a request: it has a variable scope of its own. Anything that needs to be a real one - a
  page's <code>.php</code> half in scope for its <code>.pad</code> half, or a reference that
  reads <code>$GLOBALS</code> - is a <a href="?pages/index">pages</a> test instead.
</p>

<table border="1" cellpadding="4" cellspacing="0">
  <tr><th>group</th><th>covers</th><th>cases</th><th>failed</th><th>status</th></tr>
  {groups}
    <tr>
      <td><a href="?sandbox/suites/{$group}">{$group}</a></td>
      <td>{$what}</td>
      <td align="right">{$cases}</td>
      <td align="right">{$failed}</td>
      <td>{$status}</td>
    </tr>
  {/groups}
</table>